#!/bin/sh
# Fail when a tracked file still names a retired workflow module, config or
# template. History lives in design docs, ADRs, research and the installer's
# legacy list, so those paths are exempt. scripts/ is exempt because this file
# lists the names.
set -eu
cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"
names='delivery_receipt
delivery_policy_validation
delivery_run_shape
delivery_validation_
validate_delivery
software_delivery_validation
reference_evaluation
reference_runs
authority_mapping
delivery_run_invariants
review_ladder
review_panel
review_terminal
run_gates
bind_merged_delivery
checkpoint_run
RUN.template
delivery-profiles
delivery-profile-scenarios
security-evidence.json
skills/_shared'
hits=$(printf '%s\n' "$names" | git grep -n -I -F -f - -- . \
  ':(exclude)docs/specs/rust-port/design' ':(exclude)docs/adr' \
  ':(exclude)docs/research' ':(exclude)assets/install/legacy.toml' \
  ':(exclude)scripts' \
  ':(exclude)docs/specs/rust-port/README.md' ':(exclude)tools/front-door/crates/config/src/managed_tests.rs' || true)
if [ -n "$hits" ]; then
  printf '%s\n' "$hits"
  echo "check-retired-names: retired names above must be removed" >&2
  exit 1
fi
